tasks.description:
**Goal:** `otter-node run` starts the REALITY listener when `[reality]` is configured and dials REALITY endpoints;

See plan section 'Task 5: Node config, wiring and commands' in 2026-11-13-m7-dpi-transports.md for files, code and steps.

**Verify:** `go test ./internal/config/ ./internal/nodecheck/ ./cmd/otter-node/ -count=1` → `ok`

```json:metadata
{"files": ["cmd/otter-node/main.go", "cmd/otter-node/main_test.go", "internal/config/config_test.go", "internal/nodecheck/check.go", "internal/nodecheck/check_test.go", "otter-server/internal/config/config.go"], "verifyCommand": "`go test ./internal/config/ ./internal/nodecheck/ ./cmd/otter-node/ -count=1` → `ok`", "acceptanceCriteria": ["`[reality]` optional; when present all of `listen`, `private_key_file`, `dest`, `server_names`, `short_ids`,", "`otter-node check` reports the REALITY key file (readable, valid) when configured.", "`run`: an internal listener on `127.0.0.1:0` serves the same mux tagged `reality`; the WSS mux is tagged `wss`;", "`otter-node reality keygen --config F` writes `[reality].private_key_file` (refuses to overwrite) and prints", "`otter-node reality-check HOST...` prints one line per host and exits non-zero if none passes.", "`otter-node netlog --config F [--limit N] [--json]` prints newest first, e.g."]}
